# SPA fallback: serve index.html for all routes that don't match a static file.
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output directory.
#
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# CAUTION: redirect rules run BEFORE static assets are served, so never add a
# rule for a path the prerenderer writes real HTML to (/CaseStudy/:slug,
# /SoftwareProduct/:slug, and every route in scripts/prerender.mjs) — the rule
# would shadow the static file. Only retired legacy paths belong here.

/StartProject  /start  301

# /Services retired — individual service pages live under the nav dropdown.
/Services  /  301

# Retired legacy paths — server-side mirrors of the client redirects in
# src/App.jsx, so old links 301 without booting the SPA first.
# Brand & Growth folded into C4 Lens.
/ServiceBrand  /Lens  301
# Ventures and Rebuild initiatives are no longer offered.
/Ventures  /  301
/Rebuild  /  301
# The Ventures-specific Terms are gone; old links go to the ToS.
/Terms  /terms-of-service  301
# /Contact is a real page again (fable pass — "The Direct Line").

# SPA routes that are NOT prerendered — they need index.html served at 200.
# Everything else on the site has its own static file (115 of them), which is
# what makes the real 404 below safe.
/welcome     /index.html  200
/hero-lab    /index.html  200
/helix-lab   /index.html  200

# Legacy alias bases. Old inbound links use /CaseStudy?slug=x and
# /SoftwareProduct?slug=x; the path itself has no static file, so without
# these the SPA never loads to perform its redirect up to the path form and
# every one of those links would 404.
/CaseStudy        /index.html  200
/SoftwareProduct  /index.html  200

# Real 404s. This used to be `/*  /index.html  200`, which returned HTTP 200
# with the homepage for every wrong URL — so any typo, dead backlink or
# crawler probe produced another copy of the front page at a new address.
# Google reads that as a soft 404 and, at worst, as duplicate content across
# unlimited URLs. Serving 404.html with a 404 status ends it.
/*  /404.html  404
